        const PART1_EXTRA = [{
            id: 'p1_extra1',
            title: 'A Celebration I Enjoyed (Christmas in Hong Kong)',
            description: 'Talk about a celebration that you really enjoyed.',
            bullets: [
                'where and when you celebrated',
                'what you did during the celebration',
                'why this celebration was so memorable'
            ],
            sampleAnswer: `"I'd like to talk about a celebration that I really enjoyed - it was Christmas. That year, I went to Hong Kong with my husband to celebrate the holiday. First of all, the Christmas atmosphere on the streets was absolutely magical. Everywhere we looked, there were beautiful lights, decorations, and Christmas trees. It felt so festive and joyful. In addition to that, we did so many wonderful things together. We took lots of photos by the seaside, walked around the shopping malls, and in the evening, we had a romantic dinner with a beautiful view. After that, we watched the stunning night view of Victoria Harbour - it was breathtaking. Finally, looking back at that celebration now, I still feel incredibly happy and sweet inside. This is mainly because it was a special time for just the two of us, away from our daily routines. It was a truly memorable and romantic experience that I will always cherish."`,
            prepareTime: 40,
            speakTime: 60
        }, {
            id: 'p1_extra2',
            title: 'Getting a Cat for My Home',
            description: 'Talk about something you would like to get for your home.',
            bullets: [
                'what you would like to get',
                'why you want it',
                'how it would benefit you or your family'
            ],
            sampleAnswer: `"I'd like to talk about something I'd like to get for my home - and interestingly, it's not a thing, it's a cat. First of all, many years ago, I had a cat. It was so adorable – it had fluffy orange fur and a round, chubby belly. Every day, spending time with it was so comforting and healing for me. It really made my life brighter. However, sadly, I lost that cat unexpectedly. It was a very painful experience for me at that time. Now, many years have passed. I have my own child, and luckily, my son also loves cats. So we are thinking about adopting a new cat to keep him company and give him a happy childhood. Finally, looking back at the days I spent with my previous cat, I still feel so warm and grateful. I truly believe my son will also have such sweet memories with a new cat in the future."`,
            prepareTime: 40,
            speakTime: 60
        }, {
            id: 'p1_extra3',
            title: 'A Presentation Experience at University',
            description: 'Talk about a time when you gave a presentation.',
            bullets: [
                'when and where you gave the presentation',
                'how you felt during the presentation',
                'what you learned from this experience'
            ],
            sampleAnswer: `"I'd like to talk about a time when I gave a presentation at university. It was actually for a department chairman – I had to present in front of a lot of important people. First of all, I remember I was extremely nervous before I went on stage. When I stood there and saw so many people looking at me, my voice started trembling. I could feel my heart beating so fast, and I was so worried that I might forget everything I had prepared. In addition to that, even though I felt really scared, I managed to finish my presentation. I just kept going and tried not to stop, even though I wasn't feeling confident at all. However, after it was over, I felt quite disappointed in myself because I thought I hadn't prepared well enough. Finally, looking back at that experience now, I realise that I actually learned something valuable from it. This is mainly because it taught me that the more I practise, the more confident I will become."`,
            prepareTime: 40,
            speakTime: 60
        }, {
            id: 'p1_extra4',
            title: 'An Important Change - Facing Fear of Public Speaking',
            description: 'Talk about an important change in your life.',
            bullets: [
                'what the change was',
                'how it happened',
                'how it has affected you'
            ],
            sampleAnswer: `"I'd like to talk about an important change in my life - it was the moment I decided to face my fear of public speaking during a university presentation. Before that, I used to avoid any situation where I had to speak in front of a large group of people. I was always afraid of making mistakes or being judged by others. However, one day, I had to give a presentation in front of the department chairman and many important people. I was extremely nervous before I went on stage. When I stood there and saw so many people looking at me, my voice started trembling. I could feel my heart beating so fast, but I managed to finish my presentation somehow. Afterwards, I felt quite disappointed in myself because I thought I hadn't prepared well enough. Looking back now, I realise that this experience actually changed me. It taught me that the more I practise, the more confident I will become."`,
            prepareTime: 40,
            speakTime: 60
        }, {
            id: 'p1_extra5',
            title: 'Becoming a Mother - An Important Life Change',
            description: 'Talk about the most important change in your life.',
            bullets: [
                'what the change was',
                'how your life changed',
                'how you feel about it now'
            ],
            sampleAnswer: `"The most important change in my life was becoming a mother. I had my baby two years ago, and it completely changed my world. At that time, I was working as an engineering clerk near my home. However, I decided to leave my job so I could stay at home and take care of my child. I was spending most of my days looking after him and watching him grow up. Now, I feel both happy and worried. My child has brought me so much joy. However, I sometimes worry that if I don't work for a long time, I might lose touch with society. That's why I am learning Portuguese and taking training courses to improve myself. Looking back, I believe this change has made me a stronger person."`,
            prepareTime: 40,
            speakTime: 60
        }, {
            id: 'p1_extra6',
            title: 'Boss Signed the Wrong Document',
            description: 'Talk about a memorable incident at work.',
            bullets: [
                'what happened',
                'how you handled it',
                'what you learned'
            ],
            sampleAnswer: `"I would like to talk about a memorable incident that occurred while I was working as an engineering clerk. One day, my boss signed an important document for the government, but he used the old signature format by mistake. When we discovered the error, he had already gone on a business trip to another city. And even worse, the next day was the final deadline for submission. We flew to his city and got him to sign again. Luckily, we managed to submit the document just before the deadline. Looking back, I learnt that staying calm under pressure is really important - and to always double-check everything before it's too late."`,
            prepareTime: 40,
            speakTime: 60
        }, {
            id: 'p1_extra7',
            title: 'A Useful Work Training Course (AURA)',
            description: 'Talk about a useful work training course you attended.',
            bullets: [
                'what the course was about',
                'what you learned',
                'how it has helped you'
            ],
            sampleAnswer: `"I'd like to talk about a useful work training course I attended last year. It was a communication skills course, and it really left a deep impression on me. First of all, the course was called AURA, which stands for Acknowledge, Understand, Repeat, and Explain. It taught us how to handle disagreements and different opinions in a constructive way, and how to eventually reach an agreement with others. In addition to that, what I found most valuable was that it gave us a clear structure to follow when communicating with people who think differently. For instance, instead of arguing, we learned to first acknowledge their point of view, then understand their feelings, repeat what they said to confirm we heard them, and finally explain our own perspective. Finally, looking back at this course now, I still find it incredibly useful - not just for work, but also for communicating with my family and friends."`,
            prepareTime: 40,
            speakTime: 60
        }, {
            id: 'p1_extra8',
            title: 'A Presentation Under Pressure',
            description: 'Talk about a presentation you gave under pressure.',
            bullets: [
                'what the presentation was about',
                'how you prepared',
                'how it went'
